            <ArticleTitle>An unusual complication of tracheoesophageal puncture for speech restoration.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>136-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Prosthetic voice rehabilitation post-laryngectomy is becoming more popular with otolaryngologists in Canada. However, as with any procedure, surgeons must be aware of potential complications. We present the first detailed report of a case in the creation of a dissecting false passage following tracheoesophageal puncture.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
